The package bundles third-party C++ headers under 'inst/include/glaze'. They
are a subset of the 'Glaze' library; the bundled commit is recorded in
'inst/include/GLAZE-COMMIT'. Only the headers needed for JSON reading and
writing are included.

Two changes were made to the upstream files, both because CRAN policy does not
allow packages to disable compiler diagnostics:

  * Lines of the form '#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored ...' and
    '#pragma clang diagnostic ignored ...' were replaced by a comment.
  * The two type aliases 'using <name> = unsigned __int128;' (in
    'util/simple_float.hpp' and 'util/zmij.hpp') were rewritten as
    '__extension__ typedef unsigned __int128 <name>;', which declares the same
    type without a pedantic warning.

Each changed line is marked with '[glazelite]'. The headers are otherwise
identical to upstream.

